{
  "source": "course-assets/hallucination/hallucination.mp4",
  "duration": 181.248,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 6.42,
      "text": "Look at this chat interface the user asks will my height playlist on Spotify help me study for chemistry"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.42,
      "end": 10.76,
      "text": "or will it distract me the AI replies great question a"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.76,
      "end": 12.66,
      "text": "2022 Stanford study of"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.24,
      "end": 19.36,
      "text": "1200 high school students found that familiar instrumental music improved recall by 18%"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.36,
      "end": 24.52,
      "text": "Researchers recommend keeping the volume below 60 decibels want me to help you build a study playlist"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.240000000000002,
      "end": 27.5,
      "text": "The study does not exist"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.5,
      "end": 30.8,
      "text": "It is incredibly easy to trust this answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.38,
      "end": 32.9,
      "text": "Stanford is a real university."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.42,
      "end": 35.9,
      "text": "The sample size of 1,200 students sounds credible."
    },
    {
      "start": 36.56,
      "end": 39.58,
      "text": "The 18% improvement is a measured, specific number."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.16,
      "end": 43.7,
      "text": "Even the 60 decibel volume recommendation feels careful and precise."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.38,
      "end": 48.64,
      "text": "These details build total confidence, yet there is no paper for you to open."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.6,
      "end": 54.04,
      "text": "A hallucination is a factual claim AI makes up that sounds true but isn't."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.04,
      "end": 59.24,
      "text": "An AI can take facts that are perfectly real and attach a single invented detail to them,"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.58,
      "end": 61.26,
      "text": "making these errors much harder to spot."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.16,
      "end": 64.16,
      "text": "This fake study did not come out of nowhere."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.74,
      "end": 67.18,
      "text": "The AI knows what a research finding should sound like."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.48,
      "end": 72.1,
      "text": "It perfectly mimics the structure and tone of academic writing, even when it completely"
    },
    {
      "start": 72.1,
      "end": 73.9,
      "text": "lacks the factual substance to report."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.9,
      "end": 78.36,
      "text": "This infographic outlines why hallucinations happen at a technical level."
    },
    {
      "start": 78.98,
      "end": 82.18,
      "text": "First, the AI learns from vast amounts of training text."
    },
    {
      "start": 82.18,
      "end": 85.06,
      "text": "That text includes mistakes, jokes, and lies,"
    },
    {
      "start": 85.48,
      "end": 87.62,
      "text": "all of which shape the patterns the system learns."
    },
    {
      "start": 88.52,
      "end": 91.4,
      "text": "Second, it builds its response one token at a time."
    },
    {
      "start": 91.86,
      "end": 93.16,
      "text": "It constantly predicts which word"
    },
    {
      "start": 93.16,
      "end": 95.36,
      "text": "is statistically most likely to come next."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.04,
      "end": 97.78,
      "text": "Third, AI is trained to be helpful."
    },
    {
      "start": 98.22,
      "end": 99.9,
      "text": "Because of this, it often keeps trying"
    },
    {
      "start": 99.9,
      "end": 101.84,
      "text": "to generate an answer and pushes forward,"
    },
    {
      "start": 102.0,
      "end": 103.62,
      "text": "even when it is unsure of the facts."
    },
    {
      "start": 104.36,
      "end": 105.94,
      "text": "Probable does not equal true."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.62,
      "end": 108.4,
      "text": "An answer can sound exactly right"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.4,
      "end": 110.36,
      "text": "because it follows learned linguistic patterns,"
    },
    {
      "start": 110.36,
      "end": 114.72,
      "text": "but predicting a likely next token does not establish that a claim is actually true."
    },
    {
      "start": 115.82,
      "end": 118.0,
      "text": "AI companies are working to reduce hallucinations."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.88,
      "end": 128.0,
      "text": "In one third-party study, the AI tools tested were about half as likely to hallucinate on the study's questions in 2026 as they were in 2024."
    },
    {
      "start": 128.6,
      "end": 133.78,
      "text": "Since hallucinations sound exactly like normal answers, questioning every single sentence is impractical."
    },
    {
      "start": 134.32,
      "end": 136.66,
      "text": "You simply have to notice when something doesn't add up."
    },
    {
      "start": 137.08,
      "end": 138.2,
      "text": "How do we check those moments?"
    },
    {
      "start": 138.2,
      "end": 139.7,
      "text": "follow these three steps."
    },
    {
      "start": 140.32,
      "end": 141.54,
      "text": "First, notice the claim."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.1,
      "end": 144.06,
      "text": "Identify the specific fact, number,"
    },
    {
      "start": 144.16,
      "end": 145.42,
      "text": "or study you want to investigate."
    },
    {
      "start": 146.1,
      "end": 147.34,
      "text": "Second, find the source."
    },
    {
      "start": 147.94,
      "end": 149.12,
      "text": "Look for the original document."
    },
    {
      "start": 149.74,
      "end": 151.96,
      "text": "A provided citation link alone isn't proof."
    },
    {
      "start": 152.34,
      "end": 153.94,
      "text": "You have to find the actual text."
    },
    {
      "start": 154.82,
      "end": 155.9,
      "text": "Third, check the match."
    },
    {
      "start": 156.66,
      "end": 158.84,
      "text": "This means confirming that the source both exists"
    },
    {
      "start": 158.84,
      "end": 160.78,
      "text": "and actually supports what the AI said."
    },
    {
      "start": 161.12,
      "end": 163.34,
      "text": "In a real-world search, failing to find a source"
    },
    {
      "start": 163.34,
      "end": 165.14,
      "text": "does not strictly prove a claim is false."
    },
    {
      "start": 165.14,
      "end": 170.48,
      "text": "It means the claim remains definitively unverified and cannot be trusted."
    },
    {
      "start": 171.32,
      "end": 174.04,
      "text": "Hallucinations sound like every other AI answer."
    },
    {
      "start": 174.58,
      "end": 177.68,
      "text": "When something doesn't add up, trace the claim to its source."
    }
  ],
